/ cancel %task%, write to %result%: the result when the task had already ended, nothing when the cancel stopped it.
Start
- goal.call(Name="Quick", Parallel=true); variable.set(Name=%quick%, Value=%!data%)
- task.wait(Task=%quick%)
- task.cancel(Task=%quick%); variable.set(Name=%ended%, Value=%!data%)
- assert.equals(Expected="quick done", Actual=%ended%, Message="an ended task's cancel answers its result")
- goal.call(Name="Slow", Parallel=true); variable.set(Name=%slow%, Value=%!data%)
- task.cancel(Task=%slow%); variable.set(Name=%stopped%, Value=%!data%)
- assert.isNull(Value=%stopped%, Message="a cancel that stopped the task answers nothing")

Quick
- goal.return(Data="quick done")

Slow
- timer.sleep(Ms=2000)
